INT. PLEA ROOM - COURTHOUSE BASEMENT - DAY

A cinderblock cell with a steel table. A buzzing light. A small high window.

PUBLIC DEFENDER ROSALIND KEMP (30s, tired blazer) sits across from her client, MARGUERITE DELACROIX-OBI (30s, orange jumpsuit, braids), and the prosecutor, ASSISTANT D.A. THELONIOUS GRAVES (50s, bow tie, folder).

ROSALIND
She'll take the deal.

GRAVES
Will she?

MARGUERITE
I'll hear it first.

GRAVES
Three years, suspended.

ROSALIND
Time served.

GRAVES
Three, suspended.

Rosalind and Marguerite glance at each other. Marguerite lays a palm flat on the table. Graves taps his folder.

MARGUERITE
And the record?

GRAVES
Sealed after five.

ROSALIND
Four.

They all lean in at once, three palms on the table. Then all three freeze, because the light flickers and goes out. In the dark, nobody moves.

The light buzzes back. They're in the same positions. Graves' bow tie is crooked.

GRAVES
(deadpan)
Five.

ROSALIND
Four and a half.

He sighs. Marguerite almost laughs. Rosalind lifts a pen.

FADE OUT.
